> # The simulated clock starts at the epoch, and moves only when told to.
> time show
1970-01-01T00:00:00Z

> time advance 90s
advanced time by 1m 30s to 1970-01-01T00:01:30Z

> time show
1970-01-01T00:01:30Z


> # A duration with a space in it has to be quoted.
> time advance '1h 30m'
advanced time by 1h 30m to 1970-01-01T01:31:30Z

> time advance 1h 30m


> # Fractions of a second show up only when there are some.
> time advance 250ms
advanced time by 250ms to 1970-01-01T01:31:30.250Z

> time advance 750ms
advanced time by 750ms to 1970-01-01T01:31:31Z


> # Durations that don't parse, and a quote that never closes.
> time advance

> time advance soon

> time advance '1h
error: missing closing quote


> # A duration that parses, but that the clock can't reach. The clock stays
> # where it was.
> time advance 1000000years
error: the simulated clock cannot go that far

> time show
1970-01-01T01:31:31Z

